obbyists Registration System - Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying of Canada (https://lobbycanada.gc.ca/app/secure/ocl/lrs/do/cmmLgPblcVw?comlogId=692181)\nciteturn12view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn7view1\",\"id\":23}); Total lines: 48\nL0:   * cite0†Skip to main content L1:   * cite1†Skip to \"About this site\" L2: \nL3: ## Search and menus\nL4: \nL5:   * cite2†Menus L6: \nL7: ## Language selection\nL8: \nL9:   * cite3†lobbycanada.gc.ca L10:   * cite4†Français L11: \nL12: Registry of Lobbyists\nL13: \nL14: ## Registrant menu\nL15: \nL16: ## You are here:\nL17: \nL18: # Monthly Communication Report\nL19: ## 382126-692181\nL20: Registrant name:  | MICHELE CADARIO\nL21: Client:  | Draganfly Inc.\nL22: Associated registration:  | cite5†779479-382126-2 L23: Communication date:  | 2026-06-23\nL24: Posted date:  | 2026-07-08\nL25: Designated Public Office Holders who participated in the communication:  | Nicolas Verrault, Deputy Director of Operations\nL26: National Defence (DND)\nL27: Ty Curran, Deputy Director General\nL28: National Defence (DND)\nL29: Wendy Hadwen, ADM\nL30: National Defence (DND)\nL31: \nL32: List of Details\nL33: Subject matter Detail\nL34: Defence Engagement with Designated Public Office Holders on Draganfly’s Canadian-made Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) platforms, with a focus on their applications for the Canadian Armed Forces (CAF)\nL35: Defence, Foreign Affairs, Government Procurement Pursuing contracts for Draganfly's Canadian-made UAV and drone technology as it relates to Canada's support toward Ukraine\nL36: Defence, Government Procurement Pursuing opportunities for Draganfly’s made-in-Canada UAV and drone technologies in securing contracts with the Canadian Armed Forces and the Government of Canada\nL37: * * *\nL38: \nL39: Date Modified:\nL40:     2026-08-18\nL41: ## About OCL\nL42: \nL43:   * cite6†Contact Us L44:   * cite3†Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying of Canada L45:   * cite7†Terms and Conditions L46: \nL47: cite0†Top of Page --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n12-Month Lobbying Activity Search - - Lobbyists Registration System - Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying of Canada (https://lobbycanada.gc.ca/app/secure/ocl/lrs/do/clntSmmrySrch)\nciteturn12view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn7view2\",\"id\":18}); Total lines: 91\nL0:   * cite0†Skip to main content L1:   * cite1†Skip to \"About this site\" L2: \nL3: ## Search and menus\nL4: \nL5:   * cite2†Menus L6: \nL7: ## Language selection\nL8: \nL9:   * cite3†lobbycanada.gc.ca L10:   * cite4†Français L11: \nL12: Registry of Lobbyists\nL13: \nL14: ## Registrant menu\nL15: \nL16: ## You are here:\nL17: \nL18: # 12-Month Lobbying Activity Search\nL19: \nL20: [Input]\nL21: \nL22: Searches any lobbying activity which has been active in the last 12 months.\nL23: \nL24: ## Keyword search\nL25: \nL26: Keyword search:\nL27: \nL28: [Input: Enter keywords] [Select]\nL29: \nL30: ## Search options\nL31: ### Who is lobbying?\nL32: \nL33: Corporation, organization or client of the consultant: [Input]\nL34: \nL35: Lobbyist or responsible officer full name: [Input]\nL36: \nL37: ### Who is being lobbied?\nL38: \nL39: Federal government institution:\nL40: \nL41: [Select]\nL42: \nL43: Designated public office holder (DPOH) full name: [Input]\nL44: \nL45: ### What is being lobbied?\nL46: \nL47: Subject matter details: [Input]\nL48: \nL49: [Button: Search] [Button: Clear]\nL50: \nL51: [Input]\nL52: ## 12-Month Lobbying Activity Search Help\nL53: \nL54: The 12-Month Lobbying Activity Search provides you with summaries of lobbying activities that have been active at any time during the past 12 months. The summaries include information found in both Registrations and Monthly Communication Reports.\nL55: \nL56: Note that Registry content is available only in the language it was entered by the system user.\nL57: ## Keyword Search\nL58: \nL59: Keyword Search allows you to perform a full text search against all documents within the registry.\nL60:   * The Keyword Search also allows you to choose between three operator types:\nL61:     1. With all of the words: Limits results to those documents which contain all of the words entered, no matter where the words are within the document.\nL62:     2. With the exact phrase: Limits results to those documents which contain the exact phrase as entered.\nL63:     3. At least one of these words: Limits results to those documents which contain one or more of the words entered.\nL64:   * Wildcard operator: Allows you to enter part of a word or miss a word from within an exact phrase. Here are some examples:\nL65:     * Partial word examples:\nL66:       * `Ste*`: Will find any document with at least one word starting with \"Ste\" such as: Steven, Steve, Stephen, etc.\nL67:       * `*mobile`: Will find any document with at least one word ending with \"mobile\" such as: automobile, snowmobile, etc.\nL68: ## Show Currently Active Summaries Only\nL69: \nL70: If this box is checked results will include only the activities which are currently registered to lobby.\nL71: ## Who is lobbying?\nL72:   * Corporation, Organization or Client of the Consultant: Searches within client, organization and corporation names as well as parent, subsidiaries, coalition members and other beneficiaries within all 12-Month Lobbying Summaries. Note: Wildcard operators can be used.\nL73:   * Lobbyist or responsible officer last name: Searches within the last name of the consultant lobbyist (within Consultant 12-month summaries) and registrants and employee lobbyists (within In-house Organization and Corporation 12-month summaries). Note: Wildcard operators can be used.\nL74:   * Lobbyist or responsible officer first name: Searches within the first name of the consultant lobbyist (within Consultant 12-month summaries) and registrants and employee lobbyists (within In-house Organization and Corporation 12-month summaries). Note: Wildcard operators can be used.\nL75: ## What is being lobbied?\nL76: \nL77:   * Subject matter details: Searches within the subject matter details and subject matter categories within all 12-month summaries. Note: Wildcard operators can be used.\nL78: ## Who is being lobbied?\nL79:   * Federal government institution: Searches for the selected government institution within all 12-month summaries. Within a 12-month summary, the government institution can be found within a registration or in a monthly communication report (i.e. (that is) the government institution of the designated public office holder who participated in the communication).\nL80:   * Designated Public Office Holder (DPOH) last name: Searches within the last name of DPOHs entered in monthly communication reports for all the 12-month summaries. Note: Wildcard operators can be used.\nL81:   * Designated Public Office Holder (DPOH) first name: Searches within the first name of DPOHs entered in monthly communication reports for all the 12-month summaries. Note: Wildcard operators can be used.\nL82: Date Modified:\nL83:     2026-08-18\nL84: ## About OCL\nL85: \nL86:   * cite5†Contact Us L87:   * cite3†Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying of Canada L88:   * cite6†Terms and Conditions L89: \nL90: cite0†Top of Page "
